<v Watson Jones>Yeah.
<v Watson Jones>是的。

00:23:41.960 --> 00:23:45.600
<v Eric Mennel>That must have been huge. That must have felt really great.
<v Eric Mennel>那一定很棒。那一定感觉非常好。

00:23:45.600 --> 00:23:50.270
<v Watson Jones>It did. I cried, actually. And I'm not really a public crier. But I cried that day.
<v Watson Jones>确实。我其实哭了。我不是一个喜欢在公共场合哭的人。但我那天哭了。

00:23:50.270 --> 00:23:50.960
<v Eric Mennel>Really?
<v Eric Mennel>真的吗？

00:23:50.960 --> 00:23:51.970
<v Watson Jones>Yeah.
<v Watson Jones>是的。

00:23:51.970 --> 00:23:52.640
<v Eric Mennel>Why?
<v Eric Mennel>为什么？

00:23:52.640 --> 00:24:05.400
<v Watson Jones>Well, partly because I was surprised. When you have a launch, there's a gamble, man. And the deepest fear is, no one comes. And the fact that I walked in, and there were-- it was a lot of people there.
<v Watson Jones>嗯，部分是因为我感到惊讶。当你有一个启动时，那是一个赌博，伙计。最深的恐惧是没人来。而我走进去，看到——那里有很多人。

00:24:05.400 --> 00:24:21.890
<v Watson Jones>I wanted to talk about this, because I need to define, why are we starting a church in a city of churches? You can drive down the street and you can see 10 of them on one block. There's a street not far from here where you can count five of them on one block.
<v Watson Jones>我想谈谈这个，因为我需要定义，为什么我们要在一个教堂林立的城市里创办教会？你可以开车在街上走，你可以看到一个街区就有10个。离这儿不远有一条街，你可以在一个街区数出五个。

00:24:21.890 --> 00:24:33.770
<v Watson Jones>And it's simply to say this. You can't have too many, number one. But number two, we are being sent-- we, as the Church of Restoration, are being sent to represent the reconciler.
<v Watson Jones>很简单就是这么说。第一，你不能有太多个。但第二，我们正被差遣——我们，作为复兴教会，正被差遣去代表那位和解者。

00:24:33.770 --> 00:24:38.050
<v AJ Smith>Amen. Can we give the Lord praise one more time for His word going forth this morning?
<v AJ Smith>阿门。我们能为祂的话语今天上午传出再一次赞美主吗？

00:24:38.050 --> 00:24:38.590
<v AJ Smith>[APPLAUSE]
<v AJ Smith>[掌声]

00:24:38.590 --> 00:24:39.780
<v AJ Smith>Amen.
<v AJ Smith>阿门。

00:24:39.780 --> 00:24:45.390
<v AJ Smith>Yeah, we maxed out. We absolutely-- we had standing room in the-- it was standing room in the back. We completely maxed out. And it was like, OK this is great.
<v AJ Smith>是的，我们爆满了。我们绝对——我们在后面有站立的空间——它是站立的空间。我们完全爆满了。当时感觉就是，OK，这太棒了。

00:24:45.390 --> 00:24:53.470
<v Leah Smith>So when I saw those people, I was like, OK, this is going to be like a regular church-type thing-- see you next week.
<v Leah Smith>所以当我看到那些人时，我就想，OK，这就像一个普通的教会类型的事情——下周见。

00:24:53.470 --> 00:24:55.790
<v Eric Mennel>Leah Smith again, AJ's wife.
<v Eric Mennel>莉亚·史密斯又开口了。

00:24:55.790 --> 00:25:10.120
<v Leah Smith>I wasn't thinking about it at that time, Eric. I wasn't thinking about church planting-- you kind of start small, and then you grow, and then you grow, and then you grow. I wasn't anticipating that, in the weeks to follow, the numbers would drop so harshly.
<v Leah Smith>埃里克，我当时没那么想。我没在想教会植堂——你先从小做起，然后成长，成长，再成长。我没想到在随后的几周里，人数会下降得这么厉害。

00:25:10.120 --> 00:25:43.430
<v Eric Mennel>The next week, only about 60 people showed up, fewer than half the launch. And then the next week was about the same, maybe even a little fewer. It turns out, a lot of the people who packed the church that first week were friends and family-- people already committed to other churches, but who came out once to show support. And so before long, Watson and AJ were back to the small group of about 30 or 40 people they had pulled in before moving into the building.
<v Eric Mennel>下周，只有大约60人出现，不到启动人数的一半。然后下一周也是差不多，甚至可能更少。原来，在第一周挤满教会的很多人是朋友和家人——那些已经承诺给其他教会，但出来露面一次以示支持的人。所以没过多久，沃森和 AJ 就回到了他们在搬进建筑物之前聚集的那30或40人的小组。

00:25:43.430 --> 00:25:55.740
<v Eric Mennel>They were a year and a half into their three-year mission and they were stuck. So they tried new tactics, more direct forms of networking. They went door to door and prayed with people in the neighborhood. They tried getting members to invite their friends to church, rather than just strangers.
<v Eric Mennel>他们的三年使命已经过去了一年半，他们被困住了。所以他们尝试了新的策略，更直接的社交形式。他们挨家挨户去，并在社区里为人们祈祷。他们尝试让成员邀请他们的朋友来教会，而不是只邀请陌生人。

00:25:55.740 --> 00:26:11.280
<v Watson Jones>We would have invite cards. And we would say, listen, let's invite them to church on this day. We had them all on MailChimp. When we had big parties, like a Christmas party, we would email them out. And we would see who read them. Very few people would even open them.
<v Watson Jones>我们会准备邀请卡。我们会说，听着，让我们邀请他们在这一天来教会。我们把他们都放在 MailChimp 里。当我们有大型聚会（比如圣诞晚会）时，我们会给他们发邮件。然后我们观察谁读了它们。很少有人甚至打开它们。

00:26:11.280 --> 00:26:15.830
<v Eric Mennel>Some people would come, visit for a week, maybe two. But they wouldn't stay.
<v Eric Mennel>有些人会来，待上一周，也许两周。但他们不会留下来。

00:26:15.830 --> 00:26:27.090
<v Watson Jones>We had good follow-up. Like, we always-- me and AJ would hand-write cards to visitors. And there would be people who would comment, like, I love this church, all this other stuff. And they just never-- they would never come back.
<v Watson Jones>我们有很好的后续跟进。就像我们总是——我和 AJ 会给访客手写卡片。会有一些人评论说，我喜欢这个教会，以及所有其他东西。但他们只是从未——他们再也没有回来过。

00:26:27.090 --> 00:26:31.210
<v Eric Mennel>All these people would visit. Why wouldn't they stay?
<v Eric Mennel>这些人都会来访。为什么他们不留下来？

